# Agreement Lifecycle

This scope computes key dates in an agreement's lifecycle:
entry into force on the day of signature, a fixed expiry date,
and the latest date by which a party must give notice of
denunciation for it to take effect before expiry.

Source pattern: EU trade agreements with a fixed end date and
a required notice period before denunciation takes effect.
Example: "This Agreement shall enter into force on the day of
its signature. It shall be applicable until 31 December 2006.
Either Party may denounce this Agreement, provided that at
least six months' notice is given."

```catala
declaration scope AgreementLifecycle:
  input signature_date content date
  input notice_period content duration
  output effective_date content date
  output expiry_date content date
  output denunciation_deadline content date
```

## Entry into force

The agreement enters into force on the day of its signature.

```catala
scope AgreementLifecycle:
  date round down
  definition effective_date equals signature_date
```

## Expiry

The agreement is applicable until 31 December 2006.

```catala
scope AgreementLifecycle:
  definition expiry_date equals |2006-12-31|
```

## Denunciation deadline

A party wishing to denounce must give notice at least
notice_period in advance of the expiry date.

```catala
scope AgreementLifecycle:
  definition denunciation_deadline equals
    expiry_date - notice_period
```
